EuclideanGeometry.inter_eq_singleton_orthogonalProjection.{u_1, u_2} {V : Type u_1} {P : Type u_2}
  [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [MetricSpace P] [NormedAddTorsor V P] {s : AffineSubspace ℝ P}
  [Nonempty ↥s] [HasOrthogonalProjection s.direction] (p : P) :
  ↑s ∩ ↑(mk' p s.directionᗮ) = {↑((orthogonalProjection s) p)}
```
***
The intersection of the subspace and the orthogonal subspace
through the given point is the `orthogonalProjection` of that point
onto the subspace.

